    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "86975477_96c71009",
        "filename": "java/dexpreopt_config.go",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 149,
      "author": {
        "id": 1550939
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-24T12:51:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ok, so we expect a directed acyclic graph (DAG) of boot images, and `visited` is to avoid recomputing the same parts multiple times, right?\n\nPlease add a comment clarifying that (with a plausible A - B - C example), and saying that we do not expect loops and we let them crash soong with a stackoverflow.",
      "parentUuid": "35883dbe_d4ab2c57",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 149,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 149,
        "endChar": 23
      },
      "revId": "eb5bb9745986780bf11555d0b9664e2431bc8744",
